{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan revised after review-plan BLOCK (4 findings):\n1. E2/E6 — defined the A/B BASELINE explicitly: a prefetch-DISABLED verifier run on the same closed ticket captured immediately before the prefetch run; request count + verdict class recorded first.\n2. G6 — reconciled with the close gate's graph=False contract: close path prefetches only the closing ticket's OWN file_impact (no subtree walk); subtree union + frequency ranking applies ONLY on the graph=True deep-review path. Coverage re-measured per entrypoint.\n3. G6 — recovery successors now attach the prefetch ONCE as a shared cached segment (not per-criterion concatenation), with prefetch bytes counted against physical_context_ceiling so an oversize prefetch shrinks the budget rather than raising.\n4. T8 — moved anti-anchoring/trust guidance into the completion_verifier.md SYSTEM PROMPT (trusted); added that file to Scope. The fenced section carries only labelled data + manifest + skeleton marker."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786084745901858001,"uuid":"ffdfeeb4-1446-4b9d-9197-7bee571c12f3"}